.TH GENUP 8 "Version 1.1.2: January 2026"
.SH NAME
genup \- update Portage tree, all installed packages, and kernel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B genup
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genup
is a utility intended to simplify the process of keeping your Gentoo system
up to date.
It must be run as root, and refuses to start while another genup run holds
\fI/run/genup.lock\fR.
When invoked, it automatically performs the following steps, in order:
.br
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
updates Portage tree & overlays; syncs \fBeix\fR(1)
(if desired)
.br
(using \fBeix-sync\fR, or \fBemaint sync --auto\fR (\fBemerge-webrsync\fR
in webrsync-gpg mode) if eix is not installed; if the deprecated \fBwebrsync-gpg\fR FEATURE is set, overlays
are first updated with \fBemaint sync --auto\fR and \fBeix-sync -w\fR is used;
skipped entirely if any repository location is read-only)
.IP \(bu 2
updates Portage user patches (if \fI/etc/portage/patches\fR is a git repository)
.br
(using \fBgit -C /etc/portage/patches pull\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
mounts \fI/boot\fR if required, and remounts writable when necessary
.br
(using \fBfindmnt\fR(8), \fBmount\fR(8), and \fBumount\fR(8))
.IP \(bu 2
removes any prior \fBemerge\fR(1) resume history
.br
(using \fBemaint --fix cleanresume\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
on aarch64, attempts to apply any pending fixups
.br
(if desired, by running \fI/etc/cron.weekly/fixup\fR; errors non-fatal)
.IP \(bu 2
ensures Portage itself is up-to-date (best effort)
.br
(using \fBemerge --oneshot --update sys-apps/portage\fR; failures are warnings)
.IP \(bu 2
ensures genup itself is up-to-date (restarting if the version changes)
.br
(using \fBemerge --oneshot app-portage/genup\fR; failures are warnings)
.IP \(bu 2
updates selected toolchain packages first (best effort)
.br
(using \fBemerge --oneshot --update\fR for
\fBsys-libs/glibc\fR,
\fBsys-devel/binutils\fR,
\fBdev-build/cmake\fR, plus
\fBsys-devel/gcc\fR in gcc mode, or
\fBllvm-core/clang\fR, \fBllvm-core/llvm\fR and \fBllvm-core/lld\fR in clang mode;
if the compiler cannot be detected, \fBgcc\fR, \fBclang\fR and \fBllvm\fR are checked;
only packages already installed are updated;
see \fB--compiler\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
checks and repairs gcc configuration if invalid (best effort)
.br
(using \fBgcc-config\fR(1), \fBenv-update\fR, and re-emerging \fBlibtool\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
attempts a preliminary @world update using \fBemtee\fR(1)
.br
(if \fBemtee\fR is installed and not disabled; failure is non-fatal)
.IP \(bu 2
updates all packages in the @world set
.br
(using \fBemerge --deep --with-bdeps=y --changed-use --update
--backtrack=50 --keep-going @world\fR, with retry logic; see
\fBPARALLEL MAKE\fR, below)
.IP \(bu 2
rebuilds live (-9999) packages (unless disabled)
.br
(using \fBemerge --exclude app-portage/genup @live-rebuild\fR; failure is fatal)
.IP \(bu 2
removes unreferenced packages (first pass)
.br
(using \fBemerge --depclean\fR; skipped if \fBwebapp-config\fR reports unused installs)
.IP \(bu 2
rebuilds packages depending on stale libraries
.br
(using \fBemerge @preserved-rebuild\fR; run twice, second pass suppressing getbinpkg)
.IP \(bu 2
updates any old \fBperl\fR(1) modules (if desired)
.br
(using \fBperl-cleaner --all\fR, if installed)
.IP \(bu 2
upgrades the kernel if possible
.br
(using \fBbuildkernel --stage-only\fR when available, which builds to the
staging area in \fI/boot\fR; otherwise \fBgenkernel all\fR, which installs
the kernel directly, removes old kernels with \fBeclean-kernel -n 2\fR if
installed, and updates the bootloader with \fBgrub-mkconfig\fR or \fBlilo\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
builds any external modules (such as those for VirtualBox), if a kernel was
built during this run
.br
(using \fBemerge @module-rebuild --exclude '*-bin'\fR; failures are warnings)
.IP \(bu 2
resolves clashing config file changes
.br
(using \fBdispatch-conf\fR; in interactive mode, or if forced and a tty is available)
.IP \(bu 2
removes unreferenced packages (second pass)
.br
(using \fBemerge --depclean\fR; skipped if \fBwebapp-config\fR reports unused installs)
.IP \(bu 2
fixes missing shared library dependencies
.br
(using \fBrevdep-rebuild\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
rebuilds packages depending on stale libraries (second pass)
.br
(using \fBemerge @preserved-rebuild\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
removes any unused source tarballs older than two weeks (if desired)
.br
(using \fBeclean --deep --time-limit=2w distfiles\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
deploys new kernel from staging (if desired and available; buildkernel only)
.br
(using \fBbuildkernel --copy-from-staging\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
updates environment settings
.br
(using \fBenv-update\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
updates the \fBeix\fR(1) package metadata (if desired)
.br
(using \fBeix-sync -0\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
runs any custom updaters in \fI/etc/genup/updaters.d\fR
.br
(each executable file is run in turn; a non-zero exit status is fatal)
.IP \(bu 2
unmounts \fI/boot\fR, or remounts it read-only, if genup changed its state
.IP \(bu 2
reports final status, including pending configuration changes, a deprecated
Portage profile, affected
GLSAs (via \fBglsa-check -t all\fR), and unread news (via
\fBeselect news list new\fR)
.PP
.RE
If a local binary package directory is found (\fIPKGDIR/Packages\fR exists),
\fB--usepkg\fR is automatically added to the relevant \fBemerge\fR(1) invocations.
.PP
The \fBgenup\fR utility can be invoked in non-interactive (default) or
interactive mode (see the \fB--ask\fR option, below).
Non-interactive mode is suitable for scripted invocation, for example
as part of a nightly \fBcron\fR(8) job (see \fBAUTOMATING GENUP\fR, below).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-ask
Prompt for confirmation during important steps of the update.
In interactive mode, failures during the @world update allow retry after
manual intervention.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-alert
Sound the terminal bell when interaction is required.
Selecting this option automatically selects \fB--ask\fR.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-buildkernel\-args\=ADDITIONAL_ARGS
Pass additional arguments to the initial
.BR buildkernel (8)
invocation used to build the kernel in the staging area.
Cannot be combined with \fB--no-kernel-upgrade\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-compiler\=MODE
Select toolchain mode: \fBauto\fR (default), \fBgcc\fR, or \fBclang\fR.
Controls which compiler packages are checked during the toolchain update step.
In \fBauto\fR mode, the compiler is detected from Portage's \fBCC\fR setting,
falling back to \fBgcc\fR if it is on the PATH (Portage's default when \fBCC\fR
is unset), otherwise \fBclang\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-dispatch\-conf
Force \fBdispatch-conf\fR(1) to be run when configuration file updates
are detected, even in non-interactive mode.
A tty is still required; without one, this step is skipped with a warning.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no\-custom\-updaters
Do not run custom updaters from
\fI/etc/genup/updaters.d\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-deploy\-from\-staging
Automatically deploy a newly built kernel from the staging area to
the EFI system partition (buildkernel only).
Cannot be combined with \fB--no-kernel-upgrade\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-email\=ADDR[,ADDR...]
Send notifications via \fBsendmail\fR to the specified comma-separated
recipient list.
Requires \fB--email-from\fR; otherwise email is disabled with a warning.
An email is sent on error (including the tail of \fI/var/log/genup.log\fR),
and on success only if there is something to report (a new or outdated
kernel, pending configuration changes, GLSAs, unread news, or unused
webapp installs).
.TP
.BR \-\-email\-from\=ADDR
Specify the sender address used for email notifications.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-emerge\-args\=ADDITIONAL_ARGS
Pass additional arguments to the main
.BR emerge (1)
@world invocation (and to \fBemtee\fR(1)).
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-no\-emtee
Do not attempt to use \fBemtee\fR(1), even if installed.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-no\-fixups
Do not run \fI/etc/cron.weekly/fixup\fR on aarch64 systems.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a short help screen and exit.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-required\-changes
Do not exit with an error if the @world update fails in non-interactive
mode because of an unresolved dependency or configuration problem
(for example an unsatisfied REQUIRED_USE constraint, a masked package,
a blocker, or a slot conflict).
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keep\-old\-distfiles
Do not purge unused source tarballs.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-no\-live\-rebuild
Do not rebuild packages in the @live-rebuild set (-9999 ebuilds).
By default this set is rebuilt on every run.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-no\-eix\-metadata\-update
Do not update eix metadata at end-of-run.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-no\-module\-rebuild
Do not rebuild external kernel modules.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-kernel\-upgrade
Do not attempt to build or deploy a new kernel.
Implied if neither \fBbuildkernel\fR nor \fBgenkernel\fR is installed.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-no\-perl\-cleaner
Do not run \fBperl-cleaner\fR(1).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-adjustment\=N
Set niceness adjustment (-20 <= N <= 19) for \fBemerge\fR(1) and
\fBbuildkernel\fR(8) operations.
The default is 19 (lowest priority).
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-no\-eix\-sync
Do not sync the repositories (\fBemaint sync --auto\fR, \fBeix-sync\fR)
at start of run, and do not pull Portage user patches.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-eix\-sync\-args\=ADDITIONAL_ARGS
Pass additional arguments to
.BR eix-sync (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status is 0 if the update completed successfully, and 1 otherwise.
.SH PARALLEL MAKE
If a non-interactive \fBemerge\fR(1) of @world, @live-rebuild,
@preserved-rebuild or @module-rebuild fails with a build error,
\fBgenup\fR will attempt to resume the build with parallelism restricted
(MAKEOPTS=-j1) and distributed compilation (distcc) disabled.
A warning is issued if this fallback is required.
Failures caused by unresolved dependencies or configuration (such as an
unsatisfied REQUIRED_USE constraint, a masked package, a blocker, or a slot
conflict) are not retried, since nothing was built.
.PP
In interactive mode, a failed @world update instead offers to resume the
emerge (with MAKEOPTS=-j1) after you have fixed the problem in another console.
.SH AUTOMATING GENUP
\fBgenup\fR may be run unattended, for example via \fBcron\fR(8).
Ensure an appropriate PATH is set.
\fBgenup\fR does not write a log file itself; redirect its output to
\fI/var/log/genup.log\fR (for example \fBgenup >> /var/log/genup.log 2>&1\fR)
so that error notification emails can include the tail of the log.
Example \fBcron\fR(8) and \fBlogrotate\fR(8) configurations are provided
with the source.
